CloudBurrow patch 10 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1192).

The bug: the emulator's HTTP server had a ReadTimeout of 15 s, which Go's
net/http applies to the whole request, headers and body, from its first
byte. A load's data is read from the body as the load runs (the multipart
upload handler reads the job, adds it, and only then reads the data), so a
load whose data took more than 15 s to arrive failed "failed to read csv:
read tcp 127.0.0.1:9051->...: i/o timeout", with whatever had arrived
unread. Measured through CloudBurrow's front with a 5.6 MB multipart CSV
upload: at 300 KiB/s it loaded, and at 150 KiB/s it failed so, after 15 s
of the data. On main's CI run 38715623235 the console's 5 MB resumable load
(TestConsoleBigQueryLoadFromAFile), which the front sends from the file it
kept, failed the same way after 15 s, where it takes under a second.
BigQuery puts no such clock on an upload.

The patch keeps 15 s for a request's headers (ReadHeaderTimeout) and for an
idle connection (IdleTimeout), which ReadTimeout set before, and puts no
clock on the body. WriteTimeout, 5 minutes from the headers, still bounds
the whole request.

